# 05 - Short and Long Press

## Objective

Create a program using an ESP32 where the system can detect a short button press and a long button press and light up the corresponding LED accordingly.

## Components Used

- ESP32
- 2 LEDs
- 2 220 Ω resistors
- Push button
- Breadboard
- Jumper wires

## Concepts

- GPIO Output
- HIGH and LOW states
- pinMode()
- INPUT_PULLUP
- digitalWrite()
- Debouncing Mechanics
- millis()
- if statements
- variables

## Wiring

- LED Anode → GPIO 23 (through a 220 Ω resistor)
- LED Cathode → GND 
- LED Anode → GPIO 21 (through a 220 Ω resistor)
- LED Cathode → GND 
- Push button pin 1 → GPIO 22
- Push button pin 2 → GND

## Expected Result

When the button is pressed the LED1 lights up. If the timespan of the button press is less than 1 second, LED2 will not light up. If 1 second has passed and the button is still held, LED2 lights up
for 1 second.

## What I Learned

- How to use millis() correctly 
- Timing without delay()
- States

